1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,067
CHILE IS OVER

2
00:00:01,067 --> 00:00:03,200
4,000 KILOMETERS LONG.

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:04,240
ON AVERAGE,

4
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,246
IT'S 177 WIDE.

5
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,540
ON ONE SIDE,

6
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:08,440
THE PACIFIC.

7
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:09,120
ON THE OTHER,

8
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:09,856
THE ANDES.

9
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:11,700
IN 1881,

10
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:12,480
CHILE AND ARGENTINA

11
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:13,260
PUT THE BORDER

12
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:14,807
ON THE HIGHEST PEAKS.

13
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:15,960
SO THAT'S THE WIDTH.

14
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:16,720
THE NORTH,

15
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,116
CHILE TOOK BY FORCE.

16
00:00:18,516 --> 00:00:20,320
IN 1879,

17
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:20,800
CHILE FOUGHT

18
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,040
BOLIVIA AND PERU

19
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:22,880
OVER A DESERT

20
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:24,127
FULL OF FERTILIZER.

21
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:25,440
CHILE'S ARMY TOOK

22
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:26,780
THE PORT OF ANTOFAGASTA

23
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:28,135
WITHOUT A FIGHT.

24
00:00:28,435 --> 00:00:29,000
CHILE WON.

25
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,905
AND TOOK BOLIVIA'S COAST.

26
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:32,120
BOLIVIA HAS BEEN

27
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:33,697
LANDLOCKED EVER SINCE.

28
00:00:34,097 --> 00:00:34,740
BUT IT STILL HAS

29
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:35,240
A NAVY.

30
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:37,320
ABOUT 5,000 STRONG.

31
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:38,660
IT PATROLS RIVERS.

32
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:39,803
AND A LAKE.

33
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,440
AND EVERY MARCH,

34
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,000
BOLIVIA HOLDS

35
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:42,880
A DAY OF THE SEA

36
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:44,485
FOR THE COAST IT LOST.

37
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:45,940
SO CHILE GOT LONG.

38
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:47,080
AND BOLIVIA GOT

39
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:48,562
A NAVY WITH NO SEA.

